I walk over to the register.
A young barista stands behind the counter.
He smiles warmly at me.
I take a deep breath.
I would like to practice a little Danish.
"Hello," the barista says.
"What can I help you with?"
I look at him.
"Hello, I would like a black coffee," I say.
"A black coffee," he says.
"Anything else?"
I look at the pastries again.
"Yes, please."
"May I please have a cinnamon roll?" I ask.
"Of course," he answers.
"Are you drinking it here, or taking it with you?" the barista asks.
"I am drinking it here," I answer.
"Excellent."
"Was that all?" he asks.
"Yes, thank you," I say and smile.
I am proud of my Danish.
